### H1: Single channel c0 drives motion

WHEN c0 is held at 0.8 and c1 to c4 are held at 0, THE system SHALL end the trial displaced from the start by a small amount, with x between -0.5 and 0.5 m.

```prediction
# relies on: none
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [-0.5, 0.5]
label = "outside"
[prediction.when]
a0 = 0.8
a1 = 0
a2 = 0
a3 = 0
a4 = 0
```

Result E1: supported (trivially). x ~ 2e-5 m for c0 and c1, -0.02 m for c2 (heading 2 deg). Constant drive does not crawl.

### H2: Travelling-wave drive moves the body forward

WHEN all five channels carry a 1 Hz sine of amplitude 1 with a phase step of 2*pi/5 between neighbouring channels, THE system SHALL end the trial with x above 0.1 m.

```prediction
